# Sole Call

A browser handicapping board for a Thoroughbred card.

Load a Brisnet single-file (or multi-part) export, optional program PDF, and an Equibase scratches feed. The board lays out past performances, money moves, and — when the file is thick enough to speak with one voice — **the card’s one race**. Most cards name none. That is the point.

Formerly Overlay Board. Version **1.43**. Runs entirely in the browser. No server, no account, no data leaves the machine.

## Use it

Open `index.html` in Safari, or enable GitHub Pages (Settings → Pages → branch `main`, folder `/`).

1. Bring in the Brisnet `.DRF` / `.csv` / `.zip`.
2. Optionally apply the track’s Changes & Scratches RSS.
3. Build the card.

## What it will name

- **The card’s one race** — a Pick that also clears every conviction bar. Most cards name none.
- **Pick** — morning-line favourite who also holds the sole highest last-three figure mean.
- **Price play** — favourite is second on career earnings per start. Separate line.

Analytical aid, not advice. No guarantee. National Problem Gambling Helpline: 1-800-522-4700.